    "source": "EN 16931-1, 6.4.2, Table 4, BR-CO-17",
    "note": "Three readings of the statement are settled here. The product is compared in absolute value rather than signed, and within one unit of the invoice currency rather than exactly, which is the slack both official artefacts of release 1.3.16 allow a party that rounds its own way; where the rate rounds to zero, or where there is no rate at all, what is asked is that the tax amount round to zero. At the boundary the two artefacts part: the UBL one admits a difference below one unit and the CII one a difference of one unit as well. A difference beyond the wider of the two readings is fatal here and a difference of exactly one unit, which only the CII artefact admits, is the second assertion and reports a warning naming UBL; conformance/rules/ledger.md measures both."
